# S16: Full LLM Chat Loop

## Objective

Wire `chat.llm.ts` into the message POST handler. Currently `messages.post.ts`
returns an echo stub reply. This sprint connects the LLM backend: ROOT reads the
full chat context, generates a real response, streams it over WS as `agent.activity`
events, then re-derives epics from the LLM-enriched conversation. Chat becomes
a real AI assistant — not a mock.

## Prerequisites

- S15 CLOSED (auth in place; user identity in context)
- `AI_PROVIDER_*` env vars (AI_PROVIDER_URL, KEY, MODEL) — factory.ts already gates on these
- `chat.llm.ts` skeleton exists; `root.llm.ts` implements `proposeEpics()`
- `factory.ts` resolves mock ↔ llm transparently

## Context

`chat-reply.ts` and `llm/chat.llm.ts` exist from S06 but are NOT integrated into
`messages.post.ts`. That route currently uses a static echo reply + `proposeEpics`.
This sprint wires the loop:
```
POST /api/chats/:id/messages
  → chat.llm.ts.reply(ctx) [or mock stub]
  → stream reply via agent.activity WS events (typing indicator feel)
  → save assistant message to DB
  → proposeEpics (unchanged)
```

